window.PET_DATA["practice/listening.json"] = {"skill":"listening","description":"Practice questions for all four PET Listening parts. Audio plays as browser speech until MP3 recordings are added to assets/audio/.","questions":[{"id":"l_prac_p1_q1","part":1,"type":"mcq","stem":"What time will the train leave?","options":["5.15","5.35","5.50"],"answer":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"M","text":"Excuse me, does this train go to Newport?"},{"speaker":"W","text":"Yes, it does. It was supposed to leave at 5.15, but there's been a delay. It's leaving at 5.35 now."},{"speaker":"M","text":"Great, thanks. That gives me time for a coffee."}],"explanation":"The train was supposed to leave at 5.15 but now leaves at 5.35."},{"id":"l_prac_p1_q2","part":1,"type":"mcq","stem":"What did the girl buy?","options":["a jacket","a scarf","a hat"],"answer":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"M","text":"Did you get anything nice in town, Emma?"},{"speaker":"W","text":"I wanted a jacket, but nothing fitted. I bought a lovely scarf instead — it was half price!"}],"explanation":"She wanted a jacket but it didn't fit, so she bought a scarf."},{"id":"l_prac_p1_q3","part":1,"type":"mcq","stem":"Where are the two friends going?","options":["to the cinema","to the park","to the sports centre"],"answer":2,"lines":[{"speaker":"W","text":"Shall we go to the cinema tonight?"},{"speaker":"M","text":"I've already seen that film. Why don't we go to the new sports centre? They've just opened a climbing wall."},{"speaker":"W","text":"Perfect — I've never tried climbing!"}],"explanation":"The boy suggests the new sports centre and the girl agrees."},{"id":"l_prac_p1_q4","part":1,"type":"mcq","stem":"What will the woman do first?","options":["finish his homework","eat dinner","go out to play"],"answer":0,"lines":[{"speaker":"M","text":"Mum, can I go and play football?"},{"speaker":"W","text":"In a minute. First, finish your homework — you can go out as soon as it's done."}],"explanation":"She says first finish the homework, then he can go out."},{"id":"l_prac_p1_q5","part":1,"type":"mcq","stem":"How will the man get to the airport?","options":["by taxi","by car with his brother","by bus"],"answer":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"W","text":"Do you want me to drive you to the airport tomorrow?"},{"speaker":"M","text":"That's kind, but my brother's taking me. He has to go that way anyway."}],"explanation":"His brother is taking him — by car."},{"id":"l_prac_p2_q1","part":2,"type":"mcq","stem":"The woman is phoning to …","options":["cancel a lesson","ask about piano lessons","complain about a teacher"],"answer":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"W","text":"Hello, I'm calling about the piano lessons you advertised. Are they still available on Tuesday evenings? My daughter plays a little, but she's never had a proper teacher."}],"explanation":"She is calling about advertised piano lessons — asking about them."},{"id":"l_prac_p2_q2","part":2,"type":"mcq","stem":"The speaker says the museum …","options":["closes at eight today","has a new space exhibition","is free for everyone"],"answer":0,"lines":[{"speaker":"M","text":"Welcome to the City Science Museum. Today we're open until eight o'clock, and the space exhibition closes this Sunday, so don't miss it. Entry is free for everyone under sixteen."}],"explanation":"He says 'today we're open until eight o'clock'."},{"id":"l_prac_p2_q3","part":2,"type":"mcq","stem":"The boy forgot to bring …","options":["his lunch","his water bottle","his ticket"],"answer":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"W","text":"Right, everyone — for tomorrow's trip, don't forget your lunch and a bottle of water."},{"speaker":"M","text":"Oh no! I left my water bottle at home. Can I buy one there?"}],"explanation":"He says he left his water bottle at home."},{"id":"l_prac_p2_q4","part":2,"type":"mcq","stem":"The weather at the weekend will be …","options":["rainy all the time","better on Saturday than Sunday","cold on both days"],"answer":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"M","text":"And now the weather. Saturday starts cloudy, but the sun comes out in the afternoon — perfect for the beach. Sunday brings rain in the morning, but it's dry and warm by the evening."}],"explanation":"Saturday afternoon is sunny; Sunday morning has rain — Saturday is better."},{"id":"l_prac_p3_q1","part":3,"type":"cloze","context":"You will hear Karen talking about a youth club's sports programme. Complete the notes.","stem":"The programme starts on ____ of October.","answer":"the third","answerAlt":["the third","third","3","the 3rd","3rd"],"refScript":"l_prac_p3_main","explanation":"Karen says it starts on the third of October."},{"id":"l_prac_p3_q2","part":3,"type":"cloze","context":"You will hear Karen talking about a youth club's sports programme. Complete the notes.","stem":"Sessions finish at ____ o'clock.","answer":"six","answerAlt":["six","6"],"refScript":"l_prac_p3_main","explanation":"They meet from four fifteen until six."},{"id":"l_prac_p3_q3","part":3,"type":"cloze","context":"You will hear Karen talking about a youth club's sports programme. Complete the notes.","stem":"The new activity this year is ____.","answer":"rock climbing","answerAlt":["rock climbing","climbing"],"refScript":"l_prac_p3_main","explanation":"'New this year — rock climbing.'"},{"id":"l_prac_p3_q4","part":3,"type":"cloze","context":"You will hear Karen talking about a youth club's sports programme. Complete the notes.","stem":"The cost for the whole term is ____ pounds.","answer":"twenty-five","answerAlt":["twenty-five","25","twenty five"],"refScript":"l_prac_p3_main","explanation":"She says the cost is twenty-five pounds for the whole term."},{"id":"l_prac_p4_q1","part":4,"type":"mcq","stem":"Joe began working as a lighthouse keeper …","options":["in 1958","in 1998","when he was forty"],"answer":0,"refScript":"l_prac_p4_main","explanation":"He started in 1958, aged 21."},{"id":"l_prac_p4_q2","part":4,"type":"mcq","stem":"In winter, Joe sometimes …","options":["couldn't leave the lighthouse for days","had to climb higher than the waves","lost contact with the ships"],"answer":0,"refScript":"l_prac_p4_main","explanation":"Storms could cut the lighthouse off from the town for days."},{"id":"l_prac_p4_q3","part":4,"type":"mcq","stem":"For Joe, the best thing about the job was …","options":["seeing the stars","helping sailors with his light","listening to the radio"],"answer":1,"refScript":"l_prac_p4_main","explanation":"He said knowing his light helped sailors was the greatest reward."}],"scripts":{"l_prac_p3_main":[{"speaker":"W","text":"Good morning, everyone, and welcome to the Riverside Youth Club. My name's Karen, and I'm going to tell you about our new sports programme."},{"speaker":"W","text":"The programme starts on the third of October — that's a Monday — and it runs for twelve weeks. We meet every Monday and Wednesday afternoon, from four fifteen until six."},{"speaker":"W","text":"This term we're offering four activities: swimming, basketball, yoga and — new this year — rock climbing. Climbing is already the most popular, so book quickly!"},{"speaker":"W","text":"The cost is twenty-five pounds for the whole term, which includes all equipment. To join, please call the office on zero-one-seven, four-four-two, eight-eight-nine — that's 01744 28899."},{"speaker":"W","text":"Places are limited to thirty students, so if you're interested, don't wait. See you in October!"}],"l_prac_p4_main":[{"speaker":"M","text":"Today I want to tell you about my grandfather, Joe, who worked as a lighthouse keeper for forty years. He started in 1958, when he was just twenty-one."},{"speaker":"M","text":"Life in a lighthouse was hard. In winter, storms could cut the lighthouse off from the town for days, and Joe had to stay inside with only his radio for company. He told me the waves were sometimes higher than the tower itself."},{"speaker":"M","text":"But he loved the job. He said the best moments were the quiet summer nights, when he could see the stars clearly and watch ships passing safely. Knowing that his light helped sailors was, for him, the greatest reward."},{"speaker":"M","text":"When he retired in 1998, the lighthouse became automatic — no keeper was needed any more. Joe visited it once a year until he died, and he always said the same thing: the sea was his home."}]}};
